#!/bin/zsh
# Show all claude-* commands and usage tips

cat <<'EOF'
Claude Code Session Manager
============================

Terminal commands:
  claude-start [name]    Start and attach to a session (default: claude)
  claude-attach [name]   Attach to an existing session
  claude-detach [name]   Detach from a session (run from another terminal)
  claude-stop [name]     Stop a session
  claude-ls              List all running sessions
  claude-help            Show this help

In-session slash commands:
  /claude-hide           Send current session to background
  /claude-ls             List all running sessions
  /claude-switch <name>  Switch to another session
  /claude-stop [name]    Stop a session

Examples:
  claude-start                Start default session
  claude-start coding         Start a "coding" session
  claude-start chat           Start a "chat" session
  claude-attach coding        Reconnect to "coding"

Notes:
  - Each session runs with Remote Control + Telegram channel
  - Closing the terminal window does NOT stop sessions
  - Use /claude-hide inside a session to go back to terminal
EOF
